{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Response Object in ASP.NET"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about response object in ASP.NET"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about web applications, their principles and basic concepts in a range of  work contexts.   Describe applications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present Passive "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use sentences in <b>simple present passive</b> or <b>present passive voice</b> when we want to stand out the function of an <b>object</b> in a sentence rather than the <b>subject</b>.  This tense is commonly used when we expect to provide explanations.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Response Object in ASP.NET is understood as the server's response or output sent to the client request."}, {"type": "example", "content": "As you may know, the Response Object is composed of some properties too; which ones do you recall?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The AppendCookie is understood as a method that adds an HTTP cookie to the intrinsic cookie collection"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When we aim to highlight the person or element that performs an action, we use <i>active voice</i>:  <br><br> \u2022\t<i><b>ASP.NET </b>processes pages and it produces a dynamic output to specify the life cycle.</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "But when it comes to highlight the role of the object in a sentence, we need to use the <i>passive voice</i>: <br><br> \u2022\t<i><b>Pages</b> are processed to specify the life cycle. <br>   \u2022\t<b>Pages</b> are processed by ASP.NET to specify the life cycle. </i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When using the passive voice the subject could be omitted, but in case you wish to mention it, you need to use the particle <b>by</b> followed by the noun."}, {"type": "text", "content": "This is the grammatical structure we need to use when building sentences in <b>simple present passive</b>: <br><br> <center> Object + Verb be + Verb in past participle + Complement</center>   <br><br>For example:<br><br> <i>   The AddHeader <b>is understood</b> as a method that adds an HTTP header to the output stream.</i>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Properties in the Response Object in ASP.NET"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The <b>Response Objec</b>t is in charge of sending output content from the server to the user in ASP.NET; in order to accomplish this, different properties are set when coding a page or application in this framework."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The chart below presents some of the most common <b>properties</b> that can be defined by the <b>Response Object</b> in ASP.NET:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Property\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Description\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Buffer</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sets values to specify if an output should be buffered or not and it is also in charge of sending the response when processing is done. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Cache Control</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Defines if the output produced by ASP can be cached by a proxy server or not. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Charset</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Attaches the HTTP character set in the Response Object. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>ContentType</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sets the HTTP MIME type of the output object.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Expires</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Specifies the length of time required before a page cached on a browser expires. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Headers</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Takes the collection of response headers.  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>IsClientConnected </b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Specifies whether the client disconnects or not from the server. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>RedirectLocation </b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Defines the values of the HTTP location header. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>SuppressContent</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sets a value specifying if it is possible to send HTTP content to the client or not. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "round trip  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an event that requires to go to the server and then return back to the server to complete a request "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should also bear in mind that Response.Redirect performs a round trip when executing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "string"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a class that symbolizes pieces of text in a sequence  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: it is used to add strings to entries at the end of the Web server log."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "web server log "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a file that records all the actions performed by the server  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: it is used to add strings to entries at the end of the Web server log."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "buffered"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when something is collected "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can mention, for instance, Clear content, which deletes all buffered HTML output. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "proxy server "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a  computer system that intercepts all the requests sent from other servers"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It specifies a header to declare if the proxy server is able to cache the output that is produced or not."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cache"}, {"type": "definition",